          "sharing": 7,
          "brand": 6,
          "conversion": 8
        },
        "reasons": {
          "hook": "Slide 1 is a dark, grey sea cave that reads cool and murky at thumbnail size, although the line 'Sicily, in November' does give place and time, and the sunlit lemons on slide 2 are the stronger opener.",
          "visual": "The lemons and the dish are clean, natural and true in colour, but the cave on slide 1 is dark and heavy, and the pasta on slide 3 sits on a flat grey plate with a blown highlight at top centre.",
          "narrative": "The sequence runs island, produce, dish, invitation, but no gesture or table slide exists, the cave has no tie to the experience, and the piece closes on a text card rather than a peak.",
          "audience": "The cover line says Sicily and the season, and slide 3 says villa, but the slides never show what the evening includes or why November, so the planning answers sit only in the caption.",
          "sharing": "'Sicily, in November' is a concrete time frame a traveller might send, and the caption is findable by place and service with palermo sicily privatechef, but the pictures give no specific moment worth passing on.",
          "brand": "Wordmark, Playfair type and margins are consistent across slides 2-4, but on slide 1 the small wordmark sits on busy rock and is hard to read, and its tagline is illegible.",
          "conversion": "Slide 4 gives one invitation, 'Request availability on risthome.it' with 'Link in bio', which matches the brand-facts wording, while slides 1 and 3 say private chef in Palermo and cooked in your villa; the card itself omits the service and "
